2026-10-31T16:25Z — new head `399231dcab526848b0d819f63b7d8039da4dd549` (commit `399231dcab`). This is the maintainer-ruled rename. The ruling (decision card cmsg_01VmuUhXU9SSUzqJYyXSmYSiRbuP92CLhJTP49oU1x8JNF, 2026-10-31T14:23Z) kept shape A and changed the stored key from `any` to `or`.

- The stored shape is now `{ or: [rule, ...] }`, applied everywhere `any` appeared: the schema member, the row-id strip, describes, TSDoc and examples, the lint readers (`filter-walk.ts`, `validate-preset-comparands.ts`, `validate-page-field-bindings.ts`), `metadata-diagnostics.ts`, tests, changeset and liveness note.
- Renamed symbols, with no aliases because nothing was released: `ViewFilterOrGroupSchema`, `ViewFilterOrGroup(Parsed)`, `isViewFilterOrGroup`, `VIEW_FILTER_OR_GROUP_KEY`. The test files are now `*-or-group.test.ts`. The branch-added lines in the json-schema manifest and authorable-surface baselines were renamed in place.
- Guidance: `or` is now the real key. `$or`, `any`, `anyOf`, `logic` and `conditions` on a rule all point to `{ or: [rule, ...] }`. A rule inside a group that carries `or` still gets the "a group cannot hold another group" refusal.
- The fail-closed interim wording from `912c4ac210` is kept unchanged apart from the key.
- Checks on this head, all exit 0:
